            "level": {
                "value": 8
            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>The winged silhouette of a descending escorite makes for a terrifying yet beautiful sight that precedes a gruesome end. This enormous fey moth has a wingspan as wide as 15 feet. Equally intimidating are their fleshless horned skull and eerie tendrils that hang from their abdomen.</p>\n<p>Escorites are portents of destruction and embodiments of the end that eventually comes to all things. With desolation as their sole priority, an escorite's mere presence accelerates entropy in the area. They irreversibly ruin their stalking grounds, the lingering dust shed by their wings preventing life from flourishing for generations to come. Ironically, however, they have no immunity to their own powers and live only a few years. They prefer it this way. After all, it's an escorite's calling to teach the inevitability of a permanent end to everything, including the immortal denizens of the First World.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
